WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.420
The time has finally come: Star Wars: The
Clone Wars is back on our screens, taking

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:09.400
its final turn on Disney+ after spending nearly
six years in the dark.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.900
Here's the first episode of Star Wars: The
Clone Wars' final season explained.

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:19.400
Entitled "The Bad Batch," this episode opens
with an epigraph that reads, "Embrace others

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:22.120
for their differences, for that makes you
whole."

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:27.200
It's then revealed that the rocky planet of
Anaxes, which holds Republic shipyards, is

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:30.300
under attack from Admiral Trench's Separatist
Forces.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.040
A massive tarantula-like being with cybernetic
enhancements, Admiral Trench and his forces

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:40.090
face the "two-pronged assault" that Mace Windu
and Anakin Skywalker lead on the ground and

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:40.880
in the air.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.420
But after weeks of battling, the Republic's
strength begins to fade.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:49.660
In efforts to break up their string of losses,
the Republic forces take a moment to evaluate

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.260
their past mistakes and come up with a new
strategy.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:57.170
Y'see, enemy forces have been consistently
outsmarting the plans of skilled clone trooper

00:00:57.170 --> 00:00:58.220
Captain Rex.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:03.140
This has left the Clones vulnerable to droid
attacks the more they use any given tactic.

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:08.200
Speaking with Mace and Anakin, Rex theorizes
that the Separatists are using analytics to

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:12.700
predict the Clones' strategy, and because
their counterattacks are so specific, they

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:14.290
must know Rex's playbook.

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:18.480
"The losses we are experiencing on Anaxas
are not commonplace."

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.800
"It's my strategy the droids know.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:21.920
My playbook!"

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:26.060
But that's only part of Rex's theory as to
why the Republic is losing.

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:30.560
As he tells Commander Cody immediately after
their meeting with the Generals, Rex believes

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:33.280
his fallen friend Echo is behind all of this.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:38.320
Commander Cody insists that it's impossible
for Echo to be alive given that he died at

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:43.060
the Citadel on Lola Sayu when trying to secure
transport and escape enemy forces.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:48.420
As a reminder, this all happened on season
3, during the 2011 episode "Counterattack."

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:53.720
Captain Rex continues on nonetheless, explaining
that the way the droids are countering the

00:01:53.730 --> 00:01:58.560
Republic on Anaxes implies they know his strategies,
which are all battle plans that he and Echo

00:01:58.560 --> 00:01:59.800
drew up together.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:05.340
Though Commander Cody is firm in his belief
that it's impossible Echo is alive, Rex says

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:08.860
that "Echo's fingerprints are all over" the
Separatist strategies.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:13.620
He posits that Echo has been brainwashed in
some way, forced to hand over to the Separatists

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.480
every move the Clones would make.

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:20.879
From there, Rex and Cody round up a small
crew of Clones to lead to the Separatist Cyber

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:23.480
Center and discover the truth behind the situation.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:29.219
The group is Clone Force 99, better known
as "the Bad Batch," a foursome of mutant clone

00:02:29.220 --> 00:02:32.580
troopers comprised of Crosshair, Hunter, Tech,
and Wrecker.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:36.879
They each have their own quirks Crosshair
isn't "much of a conversationalist" but is

00:02:36.879 --> 00:02:42.220
an expert marksman, while Tech could talk
someone's ear off about random facts and form

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:46.980
a tense dynamic with Captain Rex and Commander
Cody, whom they call "regs."

00:02:46.980 --> 00:02:52.459
The usual action and intensity ensues as Rex,
Cody, and the Bad Batch face off against a

00:02:52.459 --> 00:02:57.340
pack of battle droids and a sea of creepy-crawling
robo-spiders, which leaves Cody wounded.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:02.060
When that fight is over and a minor spat is
had in the aftermath, the crew agrees to follow

00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:04.800
Captain Rex's plan to infiltrate the Cyber
Center.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.920
They soon take hold of an outpost near the
Cyber Center, blasting Separatist droids left

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:11.980
and right as the background music swells.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:16.560
Admiral Trench states that the Clones must
"know about the algorithm" since there's no

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:18.740
clear advantage to seizing the outpost.

00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:23.739
After Tech and Rex make their way into a hub
of the outpost, Tech taps into the Separatists'

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:27.280
computers and analyzes its data per Rex's
instructions.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:32.859
He locates the particular program Rex mentions
which turns out to not be a program at all,

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:38.180
but instead a live signal originating from
Skako Minor, a planet controlled by the Techno

00:03:38.180 --> 00:03:38.920
Union.

00:03:38.920 --> 00:03:44.200
An analysis of the audio transmission uncovers
a shocking truth: the individual who sent

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:48.540
it bears the operating number CT-1409, Echo's
number.

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:53.340
The closing moments of Star Wars: The Clone
Wars season 7, episode 1 double down on what's

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:58.600
going on: Echo is alive, and has indeed been
relaying the Clones' tactics to the Separatists.

00:03:58.780 --> 00:04:00.200
"That number, Cap.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.440
What did it mean?"

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:04.060
"CT-1409.

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.220
That was Echo's number.

00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:08.940
He's alive."

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:13.820
Clearly, the biggest aspect of The Clone Wars'
final season premiere that needs unpacking

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.900
regards Echo and who he is.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:20.460
Nicknamed for his ability to follow orders
so well it seemed like he was echoing words

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:25.350
through actions, Echo was a member of the
Domino Squad a clone trooper cadet unit led

00:04:25.350 --> 00:04:30.390
by Commanding Officer Hevy and including fellow
Clones Cutup, Droidbait, and the much-loved

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:31.320
Fives.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:35.720
Stationed on Kamino, where they completed
their Citadel Challenge to graduate into the

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:41.200
Grand Army of the Republic, the Domino Squad
faced tragedy when they moved to Rishi Station

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:45.560
and were tasked, along with Captain Rex, with
protecting the Rishi moon base.

00:04:45.560 --> 00:04:49.380
Separatists struck down on them, killing the
majority of the squad.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:54.880
Only Echo and Fives remained of the Domino
Squad, and the two went on to join the 501st

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:59.840
Legion after Jedi Generals Obi-Wan Kenobi
and Anakin Skywalker commended them for their

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:02.900
bravery and promoted them to the rank of ARC
trooper.

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:09.160
On the Clone Wars season 3 episode "Counterattack,"
Echo and his 501st Legion teammates ventured

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:14.700
to Lola Sayu in efforts to rescue Jedi Master
Even Piell from prison in the Citadel and

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.900
obtain from him coordinates to the Nexus hyperspace
route.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:21.980
Piell died in the midst of the chaos, and
while attempting to escape after the mission

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:25.140
was deemed successful, Echo seemingly died
as well.

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:29.640
The Clone Wars' season 7 premiere doesn't
reveal exactly how the Separatists turned

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:34.700
Echo to the dark side, but some fans may already
know how this particular arc could play out.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:39.860
Four unfinished Clone Wars episodes surfaced
online many years ago, and they're still available

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:40.860
to watch today.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:46.380
The episodes make up wait for it the "Bad
Batch" arc, and one installment is essentially

00:05:46.380 --> 00:05:51.680
the exact same episode as the Clone Wars season
7 premiere currently streaming on Disney+.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:56.780
This has led fans to believe that perhaps
some or all of the previously leaked episodes

00:05:56.780 --> 00:06:00.680
were completed for inclusion in the Clone
Wars season 7 bundle.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:06.060
If this is the case, well, the revelation
that Echo is alive is only the start of serious

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:07.620
trouble yet to come.

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:13.560
Star Wars: The Clone Wars season 7 will return
with episode 2, "A Distant Echo", on Friday,

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:14.600
February 28.

